- A cell of code: a body of a function, a button that runs it, how long it took
- and what it returned. The thing a person in hitolama builds everything out of.
-
- Two ports for the answer instead of one, and both typed: a wire carries a value
- into a port of some other part, and the ports of other parts are typed. `text`
- goes into a caption, `number` into a zoom, a width, a count. An untyped port
- would only move the guessing to the far end of the wire.
$bog_vmap_part_cell $mol_view
	- Body of a function, run with the sandbox context as `$`. What it returns is
	- the answer of the cell.
	code? \
	- Run on every edit instead of on the button. Off by default: half typed code
	- runs on every keystroke, and a half typed loop runs for ever.
	auto? false
	- The answer, as text and as a number. `NaN` is «not a number», the same as in
	- a number field, and an answer that is not a number at all reads as one.
	result_text \
	result_number +NaN
	- What the run cost, in words, and what it complained about. Empty until it
	- has run at all.
	spent \
	error \
	run? null
	sub /
		<= Code $mol_textarea
			hint \return 2 + 2
			value? <=> code?
		<= Bar $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Run $mol_button_minor
					title \Выполнить
					hint \Выполнить тело функции и отдать результат в порты
					click? <=> run? null
				<= Auto $mol_check
					title \Реактивно
					hint \Выполнять на каждую правку кода, а не по кнопке
					checked? <=> auto?
				<= Spent $mol_view
					sub / <= spent
		<= Result $mol_view
			sub / <= result_text
		<= Error $mol_view
			sub / <= error
